  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.4.0 - IRTCVideoReceiver: decoded pictures from a received video track (desktop: H.264 over Media Foundation). Desktop: audio sent before negotiation uses the peer's payload type (a Reachy Mini offers Opus as 100). RTCPeerConnectionConfig.X_SctpMaxBurst / X_SctpBurstPeriodMilliseconds (desktop data channels ~7x faster on a LAN). On SpawnDev.SIPSorcery 10.0.11, SpawnDev.MultiMedia 2.5.0, SpawnDev.SpawnJS 3.0.7. v2.3.1 - SpawnDev.SIPSorcery 10.0.10: desktop data channels handle SCTP FORWARD TSN (RFC 3758), so a peer abandoning unreliable chunks no longer stalls the association.",
